WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.160
Marvel actors dedicate a lot of themselves
to the cinematic universe they're a part of,

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:09.190
and almost everyone who's ever been a part
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe thus far

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:13.700
gave another piece of themselves to Avengers:
Endgame, arguably the biggest and most epic

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.220
superhero movie ever committed to film.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:20.500
One Endgame star, however, put hardly any
effort into their role in the epic superhero

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.500
assemblage.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.040
If you don't know by now, major spoilers ahead.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:30.740
The film's co-directors Joe and Anthony Russo
recently revealed that Natalie Portman didn't

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.620
film any new footage for Avengers: Endgame,
despite actually being fairly important for

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.620
the plot.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.700
What audiences saw of her was actually unused
footage from Thor: The Dark World.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.880
The only thing Portman did do for Endgame?

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.020
A few lines of voiceover, according to a recent
Entertainment Weekly interview with the Russo

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.020
Brothers.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:51.280
Anthony Russo further explained that Portman's
voice is heard, quote, "when she's talking

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.660
in the distance, that's it."

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:56.000
That moment comes when she's speaking with
the Asgardians, thanking them for looking

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.000
after her.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:01.460
It's something of a surprise appearance considering
her total disappearance from the MCU when

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:02.920
Thor: Ragnarok debuted.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:04.840
"Sorry to hear that Jane dumped you."

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:06.880
"She didn't dump me.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:08.780
I dumped her.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:09.940
It was a mutual dumping."

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:14.420
In Endgame, Portman's character Jane Foster
pops up during the sequences on Asgard, when

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:19.249
Thor and Rocket travel back to Thor's home
in the year 2013 to retrieve the Reality Stone

00:01:19.249 --> 00:01:21.400
as part of the Avengers' time heist mission.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:25.520
In Thor: The Dark World, Jane became the host
for the Stone when she walked through a portal

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:31.100
and came into contact with the Aether, the
dark red fluid also known as the Reality Stone.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:36.040
For months leading up to the release of Avengers:
Endgame, fans speculated that Jane might have

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:40.000
an important role to play in how Earth's Mightiest
Heroes would try to defeat Thanos.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.480
This turned out to be true…

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:45.420
though it wasn't the only theory for how Foster
might have lent a hand to the Avengers.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:49.840
Some fans thought that perhaps Jane would
return and offer her expertise in astrophysics

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.420
to help the superheroes navigate the Quantum
Realm.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.920
You might recall her reference to the Asgardian
machine she was being studied with during

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.400
Thor: The Dark World:

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.740
"That's a quantum field generator, isn't it?"

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.440
"It's a soul forge."

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:05.200
"Does a soul forge transfer molecular energy
from one place to another?"

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:06.580
"Yes."

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.120
"Quantum Field Generator."

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:13.079
This one didn't pan out, clearly, but the
funny thing is that Portman's Jane genuinely

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.560
was meant to have a more substantial impact
in Avengers: Endgame.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.299
Endgame screenwriter Stephen McFeely told
The New York Times that the first draft of

00:02:20.299 --> 00:02:25.650
the screenplay didn't see the action rewind
to The Avengers from 2012 to grab the Tesseract.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:30.140
Instead, Endgame went back to Asgard to obtain
the Reality Stone and the Space Stone:

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:49.480
In that early version of the Avengers: Endgame
script, Jane and Thor actually spoke to and

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:50.760
interacted with one another.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:55.400
Fellow scribe Christopher Markus noted that
Thor would've had long scenes with Foster.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.840
Those sequences were probably pretty awkward,
as Jane would be unknowingly talking to a

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:03.660
Thor from the future, a future where the couple
is no longer together.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.880
Plans for Avengers: Endgame obviously ended
up changing.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:11.070
While it makes sense that Jane wound up being
part of the story, it's interesting that Portman

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:15.459
returned to the MCU at all, even in the incredibly
limited capacity she did.

00:03:15.459 --> 00:03:19.840
A few years after the release of Thor: The
Dark World, Portman announced that she was

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.010
"done" with the superhero film franchise,
though she did leave things open for a possible

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:25.440
return down the line.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.140
She told The Wall Street Journal back in 2016:

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:43.640
It's unlikely at this point that Portman will
sign another Marvel contract and shoot something

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:47.620
new for the MCU, especially after Thor teamed
with the Guardians of the Galaxy at the end

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.200
of Avengers: Endgame.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:54.040
Then again, Jane Foster wielded Mjolnir for
a few years in the comics, proving that you

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:56.650
don't need to be the Odinson to be Thor.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:00.829
If Portman's ever bored and looking to buy
a few new boats a few years from now, there's

00:04:00.829 --> 00:04:04.940
probably at least a potential movie or two
where she headlines over Chris Hemsworth…

